::U2UA_L7_Q01::A personal fitness program should begin with {=a clear goal and relevant fitness component~a maximal test~equipment purchase~class ranking}

::U2UA_L7_Q02::A useful baseline may include {=current frequency, duration, perceived intensity, and habits~BMI required for grading~maximal lifting~class averages}

::U2UA_L7_Q03::Which program is most sustainable? {=One matching goal, access, schedule, preference, safety, and recovery~One requiring unavailable equipment~Daily maximal effort~One ignoring barriers}

::U2UA_L7_Q04::Repeated high RPE, declining quality, and poor recovery support {=reducing or modifying the program~increasing every FITT variable~removing recovery~ignoring the pattern}

::U2UA_L7_Q05::A strong progression rule states {=when repeated evidence would justify a gradual change~that intensity rises every session~that pain determines overload~that recovery is optional}

::U2UA_L7_Q06::A complete program monitoring plan should {=record meaningful evidence and define maintain, progress, modify, or reduce conditions~collect every possible number~compare classmates~treat one point as a trend}


